{"id": "EUVD-2025-206447", "enisaUuid": "9260b64f-05ee-3c90-bf9b-ed7c14d91c7f", "description": "Building a malicious file with cmd/go can cause can cause a write to an attacker-controlled file with partial control of the file content. The \"#cgo pkg-config:\" directive in a Go source file provides command-line arguments to provide to the Go pkg-config command. An attacker can provide a \"--log-file\" argument to this directive, causing pkg-config to write to an attacker-controlled location.", "datePublished": "2026-01-28T19:30:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-10T12:04:55", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://go.dev/cl/736711", "https://go.dev/issue/77100", "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/Vd2tYVM8eUc", "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-4339"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-61731"], "assigner": "Go", "epss": 0.62, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1740476e-3a49-33bf-98c8-2d41fbfc5837", "product": {"name": "cmd/go", "vendor": {"name": "Go toolchain"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.24.12"}, {"id": "addef73d-4eff-3785-b84f-d921378baf78", "product": {"name": "cmd/go", "vendor": {"name": "Go toolchain"}}, "product_version": "1.25.0 <1.25.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dbf55879-84ea-3cd7-8858-8d06e12d077d", "vendor": {"name": "Go toolchain"}}], "isExploited": false}